From 76dd697a41d8b3cf86a5ccf1a66228577496d597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Never bridge an archive gap in market statistics

previous_close took the prior archived row and calendar returns took the
last close on or before the lookback date, however old either was. A hole
in the price archive therefore labelled a months-old close as the
previous session or as the one-month baseline. Both now require a session
within 10 calendar days, the longest market closure seen in the archives.
Current archives are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
